From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: keep transport breadcrumbs off the normal console path

The functional RX interrupt fixes remain enabled, but the ESP-Hosted source
uses esp_info() for packet and interrupt breadcrumbs.  On the ESP32-P4 NOMMU
target that formatting and console work competes with SDIO and Dropbear.
Lower only this translation unit's informational breadcrumbs to the debug
level; error and warning reports remain visible.

After 0005/0013 the include list has linux/delay.h and linux/ktime.h between
utils.h and linux/mutex.h; keep the remapping immediately after utils.h so
every later esp_info() call in this file is demoted.

---
 sdio/esp_sdio.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sdio/esp_sdio.c b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -8,5 +8,7 @@
 #include "utils.h"
+#undef esp_info
+#define esp_info(format, ...) esp_logger(ESP_DEBUG, __func__, format, ##__VA_ARGS__)
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/ktime.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/mmc/sdio.h>
